TI  - Minimizing R0 for in-host virus model with periodic combination antiviral therapy
PY  - 2016
T2  - Discrete and Continuous Dynamical Systems - Series B
VL  - 21
IS  - 10
SP  - 3315
EP  - 3330
DO  - 10.3934/dcdsb.2016099
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85008627152&doi=10.3934%2fdcdsb.2016099&partnerID=40&md5=cf79e59b0d7349c09427860417d6c407
AB  - The aim of this article is to provide formulas and properties of the basic reproduction number, R0, for a within-host virus model with periodic combination drug treatment. In particular, we extend and further results about how the phase difference between drug treatment can critically affect the asymptotic dynamics of model and corresponding R0. Our main theorem establishes that R0 is minimized for out-of-phase efficacies and maximized for in-phase efficacies in a special case where drug efficacies are "bang-bang" functions.
