AB  - The proceedings contain 27 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Applications to Biological Sciences, Applications to Physical Sciences and Applied Analysis. The topics include: Modeling and dynamics of predator prey systems on a circular domain; one dimensional maps as population and evolutionary dynamic models; an SIR model with nonlinear incidence rate and holling type iii treatment rate; dynamic complexities in a pest control model with birth pulses; a special class of Lotka-volterra models of bacteria-virus infection networks; plant disease propagation in a striped periodic medium; a within-host model of dengue viral infection dynamics; stabilization of prey predator model via feedback control; graph theoretic concepts in the study of biological networks; some algebraic aspects and evolution of genetic code; solution of viscous burgers equation using a new flux based scheme; on the wave equations of Kirchhoff-Narasimha and carrier; some solutions of generalised variable coefficients KdV equation by classical lie approach; best simultaneous approximation in quotient spaces; some integral inequalities for log-preinvex functions; note on convex functionals in the dual spaces of nonreflexive banach spaces; nonlinear aspects of certain linear phenomena in banach spaces and some results on fixed points of weak contractions for non compatible mappings via (E.A)-like property.
